In the fourth beta of iOS 27.2, Apple updated the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-music/">Apple Music</a> icon. The new icon is black and white, replacing the prior red and white icon.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/apple-music-icon.jpg" alt="" width="616" height="347" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1070726" /><br/>
In light mode, the logo is black on a white background, and in dark mode, it's white on a black background.<br/>
<br/>
The refreshed Music app icon comes after Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/06/apple-music-is-getting-a-new-logo/">debuted a new Apple Music logo</a> in an earlier version of iOS 27.2 and in marketing materials for its recent &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj; Hall announcement.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/apple-music-new-logo-red.jpg" alt="" width="1672" height="941" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1068878" /><br/>
